──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Q1. Tell me about your project.
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER (say this confidently, 1–2 minutes max):

  "I built an AI-powered Resume Builder called ResumeAI. It helps job seekers
   create ATS-optimized resumes using Google's Gemini AI. The app allows users
   to build resumes from scratch, import existing PDFs, or generate a role-
   specific resume automatically. It integrates Firebase for user authentication
   and cloud storage, and uses the Gemini API to provide features like
   AI-written summaries, job-specific tailoring, ATS scoring, cover letter
   generation, and skill suggestions. The project is deployed on Vercel and
   is fully production-ready with user accounts, admin controls, and
   offline support."

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Q2. What problem does your project solve?
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER:
  "Most job seekers don't know how Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS) work.
   ATS software filters resumes before any human sees them. My project helps
   users build resumes that pass those filters by analyzing keywords, scoring
   their resume out of 100, and using AI to rewrite content in an ATS-friendly
   format. It also reduces the time to build a professional resume from hours
   to minutes by automating the writing process with AI."

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Q3. What technologies / tech stack did you use?
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER:
  "The project is built with React 19 and TypeScript for the frontend,
   bundled with Vite which is a fast modern build tool. For styling I used
   Tailwind CSS with Framer Motion for animations. The backend services use
   Firebase — specifically Firebase Authentication for user login and
   Firestore (a NoSQL cloud database) for storing resumes. The AI features
   are powered by Google's Gemini API — I used three model tiers:
   gemini-2.5-flash-lite for fast tasks, gemini-2.5-flash for parsing,
   and gemini-2.5-pro for deep ATS analysis. For PDF functionality I used
   jsPDF, html2canvas, and pdfmake for export, and PDF.js for importing
   and reading uploaded PDFs."

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Q4. Why did you choose React over other frameworks?
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER:
  "React's component-based architecture was perfect for this project because
   a resume builder has many reusable sections — each section like Education,
   Experience, and Projects is a separate component. React's virtual DOM
   ensures fast re-rendering whenever resume data changes, which gives a
   smooth live-preview experience. React also has a huge ecosystem — libraries
   like Framer Motion, Recharts, and react-to-print integrate easily with it."

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Q5. Why did you use TypeScript instead of JavaScript?
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER:
  "TypeScript adds static type checking on top of JavaScript. In my project,
   the resume data has a very strict structure — PersonalInfo, Education,
   Experience, Projects — each defined as TypeScript interfaces. This means
   if I accidentally pass the wrong data type to a component, TypeScript
   catches it at compile time before the app even runs, not at runtime.
   This reduced bugs significantly during development."

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Q6. Why did you use Firebase?
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER:
  "Firebase gave me a complete backend without having to write server-side
   code. Firebase Authentication handles secure login with both email/password
   and Google OAuth out of the box. Firestore is a real-time NoSQL database
   that stores resumes per user. I also enabled Firestore's offline persistence,
   which means the app continues to work even if the user loses their internet
   connection — data syncs back automatically when they reconnect. This was
   important for a better user experience."

