Q21. What was the biggest challenge you faced in this project?
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANSWER:
  "The most challenging part was managing API costs and rate limits for the
   Gemini API. Every AI call costs money, and excessive rapid requests could
   hit rate limits. I solved this with a three-part strategy: first, I
   implemented a caching layer using localStorage so repeated identical
   requests never hit the API. Second, I built an AI tracking service
   that monitors usage and enforces rate limits. Third, I chose the right
   model tier for each task — expensive models only for deep analysis, and
   faster/cheaper models for simple tasks. This made the project both
   cost-efficient and reliable."

