                      SECTION 4 — TIPS TO IMPRESS THE INTERVIEWER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ✅ Always explain HOW your code works, not just WHAT it does.
  ✅ Mention real problems you solved (API cost, security, offline support).
  ✅ If asked something you don't know, say: "I haven't explored that deeply,
     but from what I understand, it works by [best guess]. I'd research it
     further." — honesty is respected.
  ✅ Use terms like "I chose X because Y" — shows you make deliberate decisions.
  ✅ Mention deployment — it shows you take projects to completion.
  ✅ If they ask about testing — say "I did manual testing and would add unit
     tests using Jest and React Testing Library in the next iteration."
  ✅ Don't say "I just copied code from Stack Overflow." Say: "I researched
     the documentation and implemented the solution after understanding it."
  ✅ Be enthusiastic — interviewers notice when candidates are genuinely
     proud of their work.

